.TH DRAGONGL_SERVER 1 "@DRAGONGL_RELEASE_DATE@" "Dragon GL @DRAGONGL_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dragongl_server \- Dragon GL master game server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dragongl_server
.RB [ \-P | \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-D | \-\-data\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-S | \-\-state\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-password\-file
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-dm\-password\-file
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-tls\-cert
.I file
.B \-\-tls\-key
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dragongl_server
is the authoritative server of the Dragon GL client/server dungeon crawler.
It generates and maintains the master world (a 300x300 dungeon spanning
101 floors), runs monster AI, resolves combat, and synchronizes the game
state with all connected clients over TLS 1.3.
.PP
The server listens on port
.B 8080
unless changed with
.BR \-\-port .
It does not start without a server access password.
.SH SECURITY
.IP \- 2
Passwords are never accepted on the command line (\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR,
\fB\-d\fR and \fB\-\-dm\-password\fR are refused). They come from a file or from
the environment; the server wipes the environment values at start-up.
Server passwords have 8\(en63 printable ASCII characters without spaces.
.IP \- 2
The server access password is kept only as a keyed BLAKE2b digest and
compared in constant time.
.IP \- 2
Character passwords are stored as Argon2id hashes (libsodium) created with
the character; the plaintext is verified once per login and wiped.
.IP \- 2
The privileged
.B dm
account exists only if a Dungeon Master password is configured; that
password is kept as an Argon2id hash.
.IP \- 2
Usernames are restricted to 1\(en16 alphanumeric/underscore characters
(they are used to build file names). A character can be online only once.
.IP \- 2
Control characters are removed from text commands, so chat cannot carry
terminal escape sequences.
.IP \- 2
Every connection is TLS 1.3 with the ALPN protocol
.BR dragongl/@DRAGONGL_PROTOCOL_VERSION@ ;
older TLS versions, plaintext connections and clients of another
protocol version fail the handshake. The server logs the SHA-256
fingerprint of its certificate at start-up: give it to the players, so
they can check it at their first connection (clients record it and refuse
a different certificate later).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-port " \fIport\fR"
TCP port to listen on (default 8080).
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-data\-dir " \fIdir\fR"
Read-only directory of the JSON datasets (bestiary, items, spells). The
server never writes there. When not given, the server uses
.BR DRAGONGL_DATA_DIR ,
else the
.I data/
directory of the source tree when the binary runs from a build directory
inside it (it must contain
.IR bestiary.json ),
else
.I @DRAGONGL_PKGDATADIR@/data
(installed). The current directory is never searched.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-state\-dir " \fIdir\fR"
Directory for everything the server writes (see
.BR FILES ).
It is created with mode 0700 if missing, and locked: a second server on
the same directory is refused. Default:
.BR DRAGONGL_STATE_DIR ,
else
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/dragongl ,
else
.IR ~/.local/state/dragongl .
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-file " file"
Read the server access password from the first line of
.IR file .
A warning is printed if the file is readable by group or others.
.TP
.BI \-\-dm\-password\-file " file"
Read the Dungeon Master password from the first line of
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-\-tls\-cert " file" " \-\-tls\-key " file
The TLS certificate (PEM, followed by its chain if any) and its private
key. Both or neither: without them the server uses
.I tls/server.crt
and
.I tls/server.key
of the state directory, and creates them at the first start (an ECDSA
P-256 key and a self-signed certificate for the host name, valid 10
years). A warning is printed if the key is readable by group or others.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-commands
Write the reference of the game commands (Markdown, generated from the
command table) to standard output and exit. It must be the only argument.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_SERVER_PASSWORD
Server access password, used when
.B \-\-password\-file
is not given. Required.
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_DATA_DIR
Data directory, used when
.B \-\-data\-dir
is not given.
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_STATE_DIR
State directory, used when
.B \-\-state\-dir
is not given.
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_DM_PASSWORD
Dungeon Master password, used when
.B \-\-dm\-password\-file
is not given. Optional: without it the
.B dm
account is disabled.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on a normal shutdown (SIGINT/SIGTERM: characters online are saved first),
.B 1
on a start-up error (port in use, invalid game data, the new world cannot
be saved),
.B 2
on a configuration error: invalid options, a missing or invalid password,
a state directory that cannot be used or is locked by another server, no
game data. The systemd unit does not restart the server after status 2.
.SH FILES
All paths are relative to the state directory. Binary files use a
portable format: fields are stored one by one in little-endian order, in
a container with a magic number, a format version and a CRC-32; a file of
another version or a corrupt file is never half-loaded.
.TP
.IR world.dat ", " npcs.dat
World and NPCs. They are a pair: if either is missing or unreadable the
server generates a new world. Saved every minute and at shutdown.
.TP
.I artifacts.dat
Unique artifacts that already dropped.
.TP
.I saves/<user>.save
Characters. An unreadable save refuses the login and is kept untouched.
.TP
.I saves/tombstone_*.dat
Tombstones of dead characters (they expire after 24 hours).
.TP
.I maps/
Floor dumps and PDF maps created by the DM commands dm_pdf and dm_mapfloor.
The PDF generator runs in the background; the DM is notified when it ends.
.TP
.I combat_log.json
Tactical combat log (rotated to combat_log.json.1).
.TP
.I server.lock
Locked by the running server.
.TP
.IR tls/server.crt ", " tls/server.key
The server's TLS identity, created at the first start (key mode 0600,
directory 0700). Keep them with the world: with a new certificate every
client refuses the server until the player removes its entry from
.IR known_servers ;
removing both files makes the server create a new identity. Its
fingerprint:
.B openssl x509 \-in tls/server.crt \-noout \-fingerprint \-sha256
.SH SYSTEMD SERVICE
The package installs
.BR dragongl-server.service ,
which runs the server under a transient unprivileged user
.RB ( DynamicUser= )
with the state directory
.I /var/lib/dragongl
and a strict sandbox. Its environment file
.I @DRAGONGL_SYSCONFDIR@/dragongl/dragongl-server.conf
(mode 0600) sets
.BR DRAGONGL_SERVER_PASSWORD ,
.B DRAGONGL_DM_PASSWORD
and
.B DRAGONGL_SERVER_ARGS
(extra options). The TLS identity is created in
.IR /var/lib/dragongl/tls .
A certificate of your own goes in through systemd credentials, since the
dynamic user cannot read files of other users: a drop-in with
.B LoadCredential=tls.crt:/etc/dragongl/tls.crt
and
.BR LoadCredential=tls.key:/etc/dragongl/tls.key ,
and
.B "\-\-tls\-cert /run/credentials/dragongl-server.service/tls.crt \-\-tls\-key /run/credentials/dragongl-server.service/tls.key"
in
.BR DRAGONGL_SERVER_ARGS .
Start it with
.BR "systemctl enable \-\-now dragongl-server" ;
stop it before running
.BR "dragongl-reset-world \-S /var/lib/dragongl" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dragongl_client (1),
.BR dragongl-server (1),
.BR dragongl-reset-world (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Nicola Taibi <nicola.taibi.1967@gmail.com>
